<description>
Count the two upper quadrant control regions to size an output made from the lower quadrant pattern.

Input structure:
- The grid is an even square split into four equal quadrants.
- Black is the background.
- The upper-left and upper-right quadrants are control regions.
- The lower-left quadrant is a color source tile; the lower-right quadrant is either a stencil tile or empty.

Rule:
- Output height is the number of non-background pixels in the upper-left quadrant.
- Output width is the number of non-background pixels in the upper-right quadrant.
- If the lower-right stencil has foreground pixels, tile it over the output; each stencil background pixel is filled from the lower-left quadrant cell at the corresponding coarse tile position.
- If the lower-right stencil is empty, tile the lower-left quadrant directly over the output.

Key insight:
- The top quadrants specify only dimensions, while the bottom quadrants specify a two-level repeated pattern: a fine stencil and coarse fill colors.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "lower-left color source tile and lower-right stencil tile",
  "dst": "output rectangle sized by foreground counts in the upper-left and upper-right control quadrants",
  "transform": "tile the lower-right stencil; replace each stencil background pixel with the corresponding coarse lower-left color, or tile the lower-left region directly when the stencil is empty",
  "grid_shape": "height = count(upper-left foreground), width = count(upper-right foreground)"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: even square NxN, N in {4, 8, 16}; split into four equal quadrants Q = N/2
  upper_left:
    role: height control; output height = count of non-black pixels
    fg_count: 1 to Q*Q (at least 1 required); pixels can be scattered or a filled rect
    colors: mostly single-color (~86%); rarely 2-3 colors; identity irrelevant to output
    shape: non-bg pixels usually form a filled rectangle or full quadrant
  upper_right:
    role: width control; output width = count of non-black pixels
    fg_count: 1 to Q*Q (at least 1 required)
    colors: mostly single-color (~86%); rarely 2 colors; identity irrelevant to output
    shape: non-bg pixels usually form a filled rectangle or full quadrant
  lower_left:
    role: fill tile (coarse color source); must have NO black pixels
    colors: mostly solid single color (~71%); otherwise simple row/col stripes (2-3 colors); when stencil has bg, each position (r,c) for r < ceil(out_h/Q) and c < ceil(out_w/Q) is used as fill
  lower_right:
    role: stencil tile; may be all-black (empty) or contain a foreground pattern
    fg_fraction: 0.3-0.75 when non-empty [observed]; 0 when empty (1 of 7 examples)
    colors: 0-4 distinct non-black colors
  output:
    size: out_h x out_w where out_h = UL_fg_count, out_w = UR_fg_count; range 3-16
    rule: |
      if stencil empty: tile LL directly over output (LL must be all non-black)
      if stencil non-empty: tile stencil; where stencil pixel is black,
        substitute LL[r // Q, c // Q] (coarse position lookup)
    colors: union of LL colors and stencil fg colors; UL/UR colors do NOT appear in output

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (constraints are easily satisfiable forward)
  steps:
    - pick N from {4, 8, 16}; Q = N/2
    - decide stencil mode: empty vs non-empty
    - build lower_left (QxQ, all non-black, 1-4 colors)
    - build lower_right (QxQ; all-black if empty, else pattern with 30-75% fg)
    - choose out_h in [max(1,Q)..Q*Q], out_w in [max(1,Q)..Q*Q]; keep output area <= 256
    - fill upper_left with exactly out_h non-black pixels scattered in QxQ
    - fill upper_right with exactly out_w non-black pixels scattered in QxQ
    - if stencil non-empty with bg pixels, verify LL positions up to (ceil(out_h/Q)-1, ceil(out_w/Q)-1) are non-black (always true since LL has no black)
    - assemble 4 quadrants into NxN grid
```
